have you been able to export your  cannabinoid ingredients to europe and do  you have novel foods authorization  so we don't have novel foods opposite  authorization just yet something that  we've been looking into um that being  said you know we will be announcing the  next couple weeks  our entrance into the southeast asian  market we're going to be entering the  thai market through a licensing deal  thailand has really clear regulations  around the use of cbd in products now  it's a fully legal market there so we  will be working with an operator on the  ground in thailand to bring our  technology to that market so that'll be  our first  international expansion  we'll be into thailand and the southeast  asian market so we're really excited  about that this is the first uh  time i've talked about it publicly so  exciting to talk about that  very cool i think we'll  just do one more question here and wrap  it up i know you probably put you  through the ringer these last 15 minutes  i love it  so uh we got one more uh have you done  stability testing on your products and  what kind of shelf life range have you  seen  yeah so our our products have stayed on  the shelf for well over a year and i've  shown really great um stability you know  less than a few percentage points of  degradation um you know again what we do  is a couple different paths so we left  their products on the shelf they have  true stability of you know actual time  you know in a product as well as just an  ingredient on the shelf there's nothing  better than that stability test there's  also rapid stability where you can use  heated chambers to  anticipate um you know a quicker time so  maybe a month can look like a year from  a stability point of view and just  different stability chambers and then  the last way that we go about stability  tested is using a unique rapid stability  equipment where we you know basically  test um you know infused product and see  basically spin it really fast and light  particles through it to kind of  anticipate how stable is something  really quickly so as opposed to even  taking a month or two months sitting on  the shelf and in a you know heated  chamber we can tell in a matter of hours  um you know generally how physically  stable  our emulsion is with a certain product  type and that goes to kind of a  customization but that's uh how uh you  know the three ways we go about  stability testing and restability you  know wrap do a rapid stability test on  any product for forage commercialized to  get that that baseline at a minimum  so  i want to thank you once again hunter  for that wonderful talk i sure learned a  lot and it was fascinating to see your  perspective and experience  um i i believe that  many of our attendees feel the same way  so uh you know best of luck to you and  thanks again for all of your time and it  was it was a real pleasure to  hear your talk  thank you so much everybody again my  contact information is here please feel  free to to reach out and um looking  forward to  continuing this and  again thank you everybody  this has been a production of cornell  university  on the web at cornell.edu


